      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 4840250
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-29T06:43:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The intended production enforcement is at the EL2 stage after a freeze point (Thats a proprietary logic). Once freeze is applied the protected kernel is immutable, we also have a telemetry logic for post kprobe and patching attempts. For debugging freeze can be disabled on remote targets (proprietary).\n\nAny additional production policy such as restricting debugfs/tracefs access or module loading is outside of this patch. This change is only a notification of intended frozen ranges to EL2/",
      "parentUuid": "6b002a49_6f1e8c08",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 57,
        "endLine": 69,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "6aeac6a034966c676fdd33771a66a563b11ba740",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c400def_e07c5f04",
        "filename": "drivers/virt/gunyah/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-29T11:18:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "... but static keys don\u0027t freeze. Many can be toggled on and off at runtime, so how do you deal with those?\n\n\nModule loading might be disabled, but the module ELF sections aren\u0027t \"protected\" from what I can tell. Why does it make sense to enforce stage-2 permissions on the kernel image but not modules? And what about eBPF JIT regions? Presumably you\u0027d want to make sure that they are not writable either?",
      "parentUuid": "a7d367ed_f20617cf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 57,
        "endLine": 69,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "6aeac6a034966c676fdd33771a66a563b11ba740",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aafc16cb_00987bfd",
        "filename": "drivers/virt/gunyah/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 4840250
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-29T12:44:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I should clarify the meaning of freeze here.\nThe current patch freezes the layout metadata, not every future runtime text patching mechanism.\n\nAFAIK Static Keys/jump labels do not create a new executable regions, so they dont need a separate layout notification like others. So even after freeze patching can be done or denied based on EL2 policy, but its mediated.\n\nThis patch doesn\u0027t implement that mediation here.\nonly scope is initial vm layout notification.\n\nBPF/JIT is different because it can create new executable memory. If BPF and JIT are enabled they must be mediated.",
      "parentUuid": "0c400def_e07c5f04",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 57,
        "endLine": 69,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "6aeac6a034966c676fdd33771a66a563b11ba740",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
