    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c71ac31a_9f32f591",
        "filename": "drivers/virt/gunyah/gunyah_kp_el1.c",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 4840250
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-28T16:05:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the concern, The intent here is to enforce post-init kernel text/rodata integrity from El2 using S2 permissions (This comes as a part of FLEX requirement from AUTO), not to add generic ACK policy. The protection values comes from EL2 being outside EL1\u0027s write authority after layout is frozen.\n\nIntroducing a vendor specific hook will expand the kernel attack surface, since the information is security sensitive and consumed only once by Gunyah EL2, we are trying to keep handoff tightly scoped.",
      "parentUuid": "5c6c350d_274ebca8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "6aeac6a034966c676fdd33771a66a563b11ba740",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c23219b7_2faafed4",
        "filename": "drivers/virt/gunyah/gunyah_kp_el1.c",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-28T22:34:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But Will\u0027s question stands, why can\u0027t you do this late_inicall_sync() from a vendor module? It would still call into gunyah where the EL2 magic would occur. This doesn\u0027t require a new hook, it just requires moving all of this to your gunyah GKI module (no increase in attack surface). Then we wouldn\u0027t need any gunyah-specific code in the core kernel.\n\nI think your answer is that it would require adding `_stext, _etext, __start_rodata, __end_rodata, _sdata, _edata, __bss_start` and `__bss_stop` symbols to the KMI and adding this small bit of \"snake oil\" is better than polluting the KMI with symbols that are not needed otherwise.\n\nWill, which is worse in your view?",
      "parentUuid": "c71ac31a_9f32f591",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "6aeac6a034966c676fdd33771a66a563b11ba740",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f1b09b6e_fb935251",
        "filename": "drivers/virt/gunyah/gunyah_kp_el1.c",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-29T11:18:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "tbh, I find the whole thing bizarre. We\u0027re going out of our way to limit the stage-2 permissions for a small portion of memory, yet the rest of DRAM appears to be RWX at stage-2? So a determined attacker could presumably copy the kernel image to another piece of memory, then change the stage-1 page-table to map that instead. Game over...\n\nOn the topic of those symbols, it looks to me like `drivers/android/debug_kinfo.c` already has code to copy them into a reserved memory region. Perhaps that\u0027s a better way to handle this? (i.e. just have Gunyah pull them out of there)",
      "parentUuid": "c23219b7_2faafed4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "6aeac6a034966c676fdd33771a66a563b11ba740",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d9118019_bb8258cb",
        "filename": "drivers/virt/gunyah/gunyah_kp_el1.c",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 4840250
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-29T11:33:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Valid concern if whole DDR is RWX at S2\nWe are moving away from RWX S2 for protected guests, in gunyah, So the attack is not possible here.\n\nOn debug_kinfo side,\nis purely diagnostic data, not a trusted protection contract by itself.",
      "parentUuid": "f1b09b6e_fb935251",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "6aeac6a034966c676fdd33771a66a563b11ba740",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
